                <pb facs="0956" n="812" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg812"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.937/23: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-01T19:00:00-04:00">July 1, 1929—7
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>221. Your 515, June 27, 11 a.m. Department believes that it would be well to
                    instruct Consul General at Hankow, if he considers such action advisable, to
                    take up matter with local authorities and attempt <pb facs="0957" n="813"
                        xml:id="pg813"/> to effect local settlement. In the meantime company may
                    consider it desirable to prepare formal diplomatic claim as suggested in your
                    instruction of April 22 to Hankow. Report developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
